{"variant": "minutes", "year": 1987, "month": 4, "day": 28, "slug": "divisional-restructuring-plan-2210", "variant_int": 4, "html": "<section class=\"page-banner\"><div class=\"container\"><p class=\"text-uppercase mb-1\" style=\"color:var(--gold);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.75rem\"><a href=\"/archive/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">Archive</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1987/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">1987</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1987/04/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">04</a> &rsaquo; 28</p><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase\">Meeting Minutes &bull; MIN-1987-04-5077</p><h1 style=\"font-size:clamp(1.2rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.25\">Technical Advisory Board — Divisional Restructuring Plan</h1><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:0\">1987-04-28 &bull; Offsite: The Dubsdread at Cog Hill, Lemont, IL</p></div></section><section style=\"padding:3rem 0;background:var(--surface)\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"row g-4\"><div class=\"col-lg-8\"><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:4px solid var(--gold);padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem\">Meeting Information</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.3rem .8rem;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem\"><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Committee</span><br><strong>Technical Advisory Board</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Date</span><br><strong>1987-04-28</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Location</span><br>Offsite: The Dubsdread at Cog Hill, Lemont, IL</div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Meeting Ref</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">MIN-1987-04-5077</code></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><span style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;padding:.2rem .5rem;background:#dcfce7;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #86efac\">&#10003; QUORUM ESTABLISHED</span><span style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">4 of 5 members present</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Attendance</h5><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Title</th><th>Role</th><th style=\"text-align:center\">Present</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Cormac Velasquez</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Director of Content Strategy</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Transaction Advisory Services (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Siobhan Black</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Vice President of Mergers &amp; Acquisitions</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Academic Advisor</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Gaylord Mccormick</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Associate, Strategy &amp; Planning</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Bankruptcy Counsel (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr style=\"opacity:.5\"><td style=\"font-weight:400\">Rangi Bishop</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Director of Cloud Strategy</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">M&amp;A Advisor (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#ccc\">&mdash;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Max Kadiri</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Vice President of Internal Audit</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Chief Ethics Officer</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Agenda</h5><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 1</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Government Affairs Update — 13 Legislation</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Cormac Velasquez introduced the Government Affairs Update — 13 Legislation, noting its importance to the company&#x27;s strategic objectives for 1987. Rangi Bishop presented three alternative approaches, detailed in Exhibit A. The committee debated the merits of each before voting on the preferred option.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 2</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">External Auditor Independence Review</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The committee discussed the External Auditor Independence Review, a review of the company&#x27;s compliance with the Sarbanes-Oxley Act (SOX). The committee reviewed the company&#x27;s internal controls over financial reporting and confirmed that they were effective.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To find:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Technical Advisory Board approves the revised compensation structure for Corporate Governance Alliance as set forth in Exhibit B, and directs management to implement the approved changes no later than 1987-06-28.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Siobhan Black &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Cormac Velasquez</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 3 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 1 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 3</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Quarterly Compensation Analysis — Corporate Governance Alliance</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Quarterly Compensation Analysis — Corporate Governance Alliance was a follow-up from the previous meeting. Gaylord Mccormick confirmed that all action items had been completed and that the issue was now resolved. The committee formally closed the item.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To approve for partnership:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Technical Advisory Board recommends that the full Board of Directors approve the Quarterly Compensation Analysis — Corporate Governance Alliance at its next scheduled meeting.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Siobhan Black &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Gaylord Mccormick</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 4 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 4</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Annual Performance Goal Setting for Executive Team</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Annual Performance Goal Setting for Executive Team was a review of the company&#x27;s DEI metrics. Gaylord Mccormick reported that representation of underrepresented groups had increased by 15% year-over-year. The committee commended the progress but noted that more work was needed.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To approve for submission:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Technical Advisory Board approves the capital expenditure of up to $124M for the Annual Performance Goal Setting for Executive Team, as detailed in the financial analysis provided in Exhibit D.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Siobhan Black &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Gaylord Mccormick</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 4 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 5</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Technology Roadmap and Investment Plan for FY1987</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The committee discussed the Technology Roadmap and Investment Plan for FY1987, a review of the company&#x27;s political and lobbying activities. The committee approved the lobbying disclosure report for the previous quarter.</p></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Action Items</h5><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th style=\"width:2rem\">#</th><th>Description</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">1</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Model the financial impact of the proposed changes to the health plan</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Shirley Coffey</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-06-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">2</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Conduct a post-implementation review of the new HRIS platform</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Birgit Zafar</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-05-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">3</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Draft a new policy on the company&#x27;s approach to stakeholder engagement</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Aleksandra Lyons</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-05-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">4</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Provide a summary of employee feedback from the recent pulse survey</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Abdullah Zimmermann</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-06-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">5</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Draft a response to the recent media inquiry regarding External Auditor Independence Review</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Tal Dasgupta</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-06-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">6</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Review and update the company&#x27;s records retention schedule</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Ilaria Hilton</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-06-28</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem 1.2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem\"><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:#333;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.5rem\">There being no further business, a motion to adjourn was made and carried unanimously. Meeting adjourned at 2:45 PM CT.</p><p style=\"font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;color:#555\"><strong>Next meeting:</strong> 1987-05-19</p><div><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#888;margin-bottom:.25rem\">Respectfully submitted,</p><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.1rem\">Max Kadiri</p><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#666;margin-bottom:.75rem\">Vice President of Internal Audit, Chief Ethics Officer</p><div style=\"display:flex;gap:2rem\"><div><div style=\"width:160px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Signature</div></div><div><div style=\"width:120px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Approved: ___________</div></div></div></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><a href=\"/archive/1987/04/27/system-access-controls-review-6943/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none\">&larr; Previous</a><a href=\"/archive/1987/04/28/divisional-restructuring-plan-2210/committee-independence-assessment-7258/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none\">Next &rarr;</a></div></div><div class=\"col-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block\"><div style=\"position:sticky;top:2rem\"><div class=\"acpwb-card mb-3\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.7rem\">Meeting Record</div><dl class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font-size:.82rem\"><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Meeting Ref</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\" style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.75rem;opacity:.7\">MIN-1987-04-5077</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Date</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">1987-04-28</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Committee</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">Technical Advisory Board</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Quorum</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\"><span s